6) Create Public Route Table ✅

Route Table Name: Public-RT-02
Purpose: Provide Internet routing for Public Subnet resources.

Activities Performed:
• Created Public-RT-02

Outcome:
✔ Public Route Table created successfully.

7) Configure Public Route Table ✅

Purpose: Enable Internet communication for Public Subnet resources.

Activities Performed:
• Added route 0.0.0.0/0 → My-IGW-02

Routes Configured:
10.0.0.0/16 → local
0.0.0.0/0   → My-IGW-02

Outcome:
✔ Internet Route configured successfully
✔ Public Internet access enabled

Notes:
0.0.0.0/0 represents all Internet destinations.

8) Associate Public Route Table ✅

Association: 

Public-Subnet-02

↓

Public-RT-02

Purpose: Make Public-Subnet-02 an Internet-accessible subnet.

Outcome:
✔ Public Route Table associated successfully
✔ Public-Subnet-02 became a Public Subnet

Important Learning ❗

A Public Subnet requires:
-Internet Gateway
-Internet Route
- Route Table Association

9) Create Private Route Table ✅

Route Table Name: Private-RT-02

Purpose: Create dedicated routing for the Private Subnet.

Activities Performed:
• Created Private-RT-02
• Retained only the local route

Routes Configured:
10.0.0.0/16 → local (Only local route).

Outcome: 
✔ Private Route Table created successfully

Important: No Internet Route was configured.

